The second moment $EE[X^2]$ determines the spread of $X$ through
$
  "Var"(X) = EE[X^2] - (EE[X])^2.
$
Derivatives of the probability generating function produce moments of this kind: $p''(1^-) = EE[X(X-1)]$ and more generally $p^((k))(1^-) = EE[X(X-1)...(X-k+1)]$, from which $"Var"(X) = p''(1^-) + p'(1^-) - (p'(1^-))^2$.
